<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στωμ-ύλλω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στωμύλος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be
				talkative, chatter, babble</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριβολεκτράπελα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					1003
				</span></i>
			; Com. of birds, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1310
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> more freq.
			in 
				Med.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στωμύλλομαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1073
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1071
			</span></i>: fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στωμῠλοῦμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1376
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐστωμῡλάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					579
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				461
			</span></i> (cj. Dind.): also in good sense, <i>talk, chat</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἀλλήλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pax</u>
					995
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
